Okay it's another bag. It's a play on words. An egg sack. Hopefully the 
drawbacks outweigh the benefits.

(a)pply the egg sack and receive one egg. One can eat the egg, keep it in 
their inventory or toss it as a weapon. Of course one must cast identify 
or read a scroll of identify to see what kind of egg was re: cockatrices.

The eggs are randomly chosen and a single egg sack will not produce 
creatures of a particular type unless by type one is thinking "all of a" 
or "all of s" but I like the random factor.

Upside is that one will have a source of pets, potential instakill items 
and a source of food meager as it may be (80 nutrition).

The downside is that one will have a source to produce hostile nasties, 
possible instakill items was re: cockatrices if someone decides to test 
gravity or eat in haste.

And add a little cruft, if someone happens to be carrying an egg sack and 
they're hit by a wand of striking then they'll hear a cracking sound 
which will revert the egg sack to a normal, everyday sack since all the 
eggs are broken. Also when the egg sack is done, it can not be recharged 
and reverts to a regular bag.

Actually I think a bag of tricks should also revert to a regular bag once 
all the charges are used up.


